# Automation Coverage — {{ project_name }}

Living ledger of test case automation status. Written by automation-agent after each
automation phase. The main agent reads this as the done-probe: when no `pending` rows
exist for a ticket's scope, the pipeline is complete.

## Format

| ticket_key | case_id | status | spec_path | test_name | notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `PROJ-1234` | `C000001` | `automated` | `tests/domain/feature.spec` | `Test title` | |
| `PROJ-1234` | `C000002` | `excluded` | | | `Reason: non-deterministic timing` |
| `PROJ-1235` | `C000003` | `pending` | | | `Automation not started` |

## Status Values

| Status | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `automated` | Spec exists, tags the case ID, passed the verification gate (lint + type-check + run) |
| `excluded` | Case is not automatable — reason must be documented in `notes` |
| `pending` | bdd-agent has published the case; automation-agent has not yet run |

## Done-Probe

The pipeline is **complete** for a ticket when:
- Every row for that `ticket_key` has status `automated` or `excluded`.
- No `pending` rows remain.

The main agent checks this table after every automation-agent run.

## Exclusion Reasons

Use one of these standardised reasons in the `notes` column for `excluded` cases:

| Reason | When to use |
|---|---|
| `non_deterministic` | Test result varies without a code change (timing, external data) |
| `human_observer_required` | Requires a person to judge correctness (visual, audio) |
| `hardware_dependency` | Requires physical hardware (NFC, camera, barcode scanner) |
| `already_covered` | Another spec already covers this case (link to the spec) |
| `failed_manual` | Case was `failed_scenario` or `blocked` in the manual run |
| `automation_gate_failed` | Passed lint + type-check but could not achieve a green run after 3 attempts |
| `out_of_scope` | Agreed with QA lead that this case will not be automated |

## Write-Back Procedure

automation-agent appends rows after each automation session. The main agent confirms
write-back via the `writeback_targets` field in the handoff contract.

Never delete rows — update the `status` column if a case changes state.
